// ============================================================================
//  mod_nukeddogs.zone - THE HELLHOUND EFFECTS, SO NUKETOWN CAN SHOW THEM.
//                                                                    (v2.2.0)
//  User, 2026-08-21: *"I played a match of nuketown survival with the new
//  hellhounds option turned on in the pre-game menu, it works but there's a
//  bunch of missing sound effects and visual effects, make sure that the dog
//  rounds on nuketown are not missing anything."*
//
//  🌟 MEASURED, NOT SUSPECTED. All five effects _zm_ai_dogs::init() loads live
//  in so_zsurvival_zm_transit.ff - the TRANZIT SURVIVAL fastfile - and in
//  nothing else that Nuketown loads:
//        Unlinker --list so_zsurvival_zm_transit.ff | grep fx_zombie_dog
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_lightning_spawn
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_lightning_buildup
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_eyes
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_explosion
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_fire_trail
//            fx, maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_ash_trail
//        the same command on zm_nuked.ff, zm_nuked_patch.ff, zm_transit.ff,
//        zm_transit_patch.ff, common_zm.ff and patch_zm.ff finds NONE of them.
//  Nuketown survival does not load a so_zsurvival fastfile - only TranZit ships
//  one - so on Nuketown every one of those loadfx() calls returns undefined and
//  playfx() has nothing to draw. No spawn lightning, no eye glow, no gib, no
//  fire trail, no ash trail. That is the "missing visual effects".
//
//  🛑 SHIPPING A STOCK-NAMED ASSET IN mod.ff IS SAFE HERE, AND THAT IS PROVEN BY
//  THIS MOD'S OWN BUILD, not assumed. mod.ff already owns
//        xmodel,  p6_zm_al_vending_ads_on          - zm_prison.ff ships it too
//        fx,      misc/fx_zombie_cola_arsenal_on   - zm_buried.ff ships it too
//  and the mod boots and plays on both of those maps. The fatal "Attempting to
//  override asset ... from zone 'mod'" case is a stock SOUND BANK declared in
//  our zone (v1.21.0, Origins), which is a different asset class entirely.
//
//  🛑 DONOR ORDER MATTERS AND IT IS ALREADY RIGHT. build_ff.bat --loads
//  so_zsurvival_zm_transit.ff fifth, and none of the four ahead of it
//  (base mod.ff, ui_zm, zm_prison, zm_prison_patch) carries any fx_zombie_dog_*
//  - checked with Unlinker --list on all four - so these resolve from the one
//  fastfile that has them and there is no per-map permutation to pick wrong.
//
//  📝 lightning_spawn is included even though _zm_ai_dogs::init() does not load
//  it: it is part of the same set in the donor and costs nothing.
// ============================================================================
>game,T6
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_lightning_buildup
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_lightning_spawn
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_eyes
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_explosion
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_fire_trail
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_dog_ash_trail

// ============================================================================
//  🛑 v2.7.2 - THE UNLOAD FREEZE REGRESSED THROUGH HERE, MEASURED NOT GUESSED.
//  fx_zombie_dog_explosion's own internal dependency chain pulls in TWO xmodels
//  that common_zm.ff ALSO owns under the identical name - fx_char_gib_chunk_fat
//  and fx_char_gib_chunk_meat02 - and because ww_donor/mod.ff and pro7_donor/
//  mod.ff (both --load'ed ahead of common_zm.ff in build_ff.bat) carry their own
//  baked copies too, the Linker had real data to bake a SECOND copy into mod.ff
//  regardless of mod_wonderweapons.zone's own (correct, but only advisory for
//  EXPLICIT top-level declarations) comment-out of these same two names.
//
//  This is exactly the asset-class collision checkpoint 85 (v1.99.82) traced the
//  original mod-unload freeze to and removed - confirmed by a class-by-class
//  audit against common_zm.ff finding these as the ONLY two xmodel collisions in
//  the whole build (zero script collisions, unlike back then). Verified with a
//  scratch relink (mod_base+locations+wonderweapons+freezefx+xpr50+titus6, then
//  adding nukeddogs alone) that mod_nukeddogs is what reintroduces them - none of
//  the other zones added since v1.99.82 touch them.
//
//  Bare-declaring them here (no data after the second comma) does NOT drop the
//  dog explosion's gib visual - fx_zombie_dog_explosion still references them by
//  name and the engine resolves that name from common_zm.ff at runtime, exactly
//  like fx_flesh_hit_splat did before common_mp.ff supplied real data for it (see
//  build_ff.bat's own load-order comment block). Confirmed with the same scratch
//  relink: with these two lines added, Unlinker --list shows
//  "xmodel, ,fx_char_gib_chunk_fat" / "xmodel, ,fx_char_gib_chunk_meat02" - a
//  bare reference, not a second copy of the mesh.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,,fx_char_gib_chunk_fat
xmodel,,fx_char_gib_chunk_meat02
